{"kind":"request","text":"BO3: consent on party slots. Third slice of the boundary-objects\ndesign note (notes/2026-10-28-boundary-objects-in-use.md, landed\n8659af46), child of request 0e06e751. After BO1. Kernel filing gate\napplies (contract definition.ts and the signer entry part).\n\nScope, as the note's slice list states it:\n1. The consent rule on party slots: signer (default), ratified,\n   declared. A slot with no consent and an effect that writes it is\n   refused consent-unstated.\n2. The signer part of EntryPart, so a presented entry's signer can be\n   read beside kind, intent, on and time.\n3. The validator's four guards for a ratified slot: consent-terms,\n   consent-item, consent-signer, and a fourth name for the terms-digest\n   guard, which the note leaves unnamed (approval 1703cf3b point 4);\n   choose it in the consent- family and add it to the note. A missing\n   ratification is consent-missing; consumption is consent-consumed,\n   with the slot holding the member and the ratification's reference\n   in the act's own entry.\n4. List slots and cleared slots (approval point 3): for a party slot\n   with list: true the guard refuses a ratification reference the list\n   already holds; if an effect can clear a slot, state what stops the\n   same ratification from being presented again, and enforce it. The\n   note's section 9 is corrected in this head.\n5. The install screen lists every declared slot with the acts that\n   write it.\n6. The first ratified slot in a package: the snag list (case 30).\n7. Witness W3 (consent before binding), the six presentations with\n   their four refusal names, the fifth taking effect and citing the\n   row's hashes, the sixth refused consent-consumed.\n\nReview cites docs/kernel.md section 7 for the contract additions.\n\nNot in this slice: closings and the matter projection (BO4).","body":{"conditions":"Review cites docs/kernel.md section 7 (consent member, signer entry part); refusal names consent-unstated, consent-missing, consent-terms, consent-item, consent-signer, consent-consumed and the named fourth guard; list and cleared slots stated and enforced; install screen lists declared slots; snag list carries the first ratified slot; witness W3 recorded with all six presentations; gate green.","target_head":"8659af4656b9289d25f239d02b22b89ae44fe658","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}